info/bugpattern/InsecureCryptoUsage) and switched off that EP check:\r\n\r\n```python\r\n java_library(\r\n     name = \"insecure_cipher_factory\",\r\n     srcs = INSECURE_CIPHER_FACTORY,\r\n     javacopts = [\"-Xep:InsecureCryptoUsage:OFF\"],\r\n )\r\n```\r\n\r\nHowever in recent Bazel releases the build is not failing, even if I remove: `javacopts` - parameter:\r\n\r\n```python\r\n java_library(\r\n     name = \"insecure_cipher_factory\",\r\n     srcs = INSECURE_CIPHER_FACTORY,\r\n )\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe error only shows up, if I swap the logic and set severity to error:\r\n\r\n```diff\r\ndiff --git a/org.eclipse.jgit/BUILD b/org.eclipse.jgit/BUILD\r\nindex 04873b0c7..20abcfb15 100644\r\n--- a/org.eclipse.jgit/BUILD\r\n+++ b/org.eclipse.jgit/BUILD\r\n@@ -49,5 +49,5 @@ genrule(\r\n java_library(\r\n     name = \"insecure_cipher_factory\",\r\n     srcs = INSECURE_CIPHER_FACTORY,\r\n-    javacopts = [\"-Xep:InsecureCryptoUsage:OFF\"],\r\n+    javacopts = [\"-Xep:InsecureCryptoUsage:ERROR\"],\r\n )\r\n```\r\n\r\nOnly then the build is failing:\r\n\r\n\r\n```bash\r\n  $ bazel build org.eclipse.jgit:insecure_cipher_factory\r\nINFO: Invocation ID: 64b1e2b1-0232-4b91-af3a-da3ff396bff5\r\nDEBUG: /home/davido/.cache/bazel/_bazel_davido/e1ee1c2b4d81e57e5c4b6fbb219eece8/external/bazel_skylib/lib/versions.bzl:96:18: Current Bazel is not a release version; cannot check for compatibility. Make sure that you are running at least Bazel 3.7.0.\r\nINFO: Analyzed target //org.eclipse.jgit:insecure_cipher_factory (1 packages loaded, 2 targets configured).\r\nINFO: Found 1 target...\r\nERROR: /home/davido/projects/jgit/org.eclipse.jgit/BUILD:49:13: Building org.eclipse.jgit/libinsecure_cipher_factory.jar (1 source file) failed: (Exit 1): java failed: error executing command external/remotejdk11_linux/bin/java -XX:-CompactStrings '--add-exports=jdk.compiler/com.sun.tools.javac.api=ALL-UNNAMED' '--add-exports=jdk.compiler/com.sun.tools.javac.code=ALL-UNNAMED' ... (remaining 14 argument(s) skipped)\r\norg.eclipse.jgit/src/org/eclipse/jgit/transport/InsecureCipherFactory.java:30: error: [InsecureCryptoUsage] Insecure usage of a crypto API: the transformation is not a compile-time constant expression.\r\n\t\treturn Cipher.getInstance(algo);\r\n\t\t                         ^\r\n    (see https://errorprone.info/bugpattern/InsecureCryptoUsage)\r\nTarget //org.eclipse.jgit:insecure_cipher_factory failed to build\r\nUse --verbose_failures to see the command lines of failed build steps.\r\nINFO: Elapsed time: 0.600s, Critical Path: 0.36s\r\nINFO: 2 processes: 2 internal.\r\nFAILED: Build did NOT complete successfully\r\n```\r\n\r\nOk, that pattern was disabled: with this CL:\r\nhttps://github.com/google/error-prone/commit/f680b794126b97ffc875eb7035a4ddb81fc879fb\r\nand referenced by: #2591.\r\n\r\n//CC @cushon @comius ","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/12795/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/12795/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]